  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 13,
  "Question": "What value of \\(x\\) makes \\(8xy - 12y + 2x - 3 = 0\\) true for all values of \\(y?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac23\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac32\\) or \\(-\\dfrac14\\)",
    "C": "\\(-\\dfrac23\\) or \\(-\\dfrac14\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac32\\)",
    "E": "\\(-\\dfrac32\\) or \\(-\\dfrac14\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The equation must hold for every value of \\(y\\), so it must hold when \\(y=0\\). This removes the terms containing \\(y\\) and gives\n\\[\n2x-3=0,\n\\]\nso \\(x=\\frac32\\).\n\nWe must also check that this value works for every \\(y\\), rather than only for \\(y=0\\). Substituting it into the original expression gives\n\\[\n8\\left(\\frac32\\right)y-12y+2\\left(\\frac32\\right)-3\n=12y-12y+3-3=0.\n\\]\nThus the unique value is \\(\\boxed{\\frac32}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
